infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Front-door check vs Data Access Layer: bypassable vs unskippable
  desc Middleware and layouts can be skipped entirely; a check attached to the data cannot
  compares
    - label Front-door check (middleware / layout)
      children
        - label Skippable by one header
          desc CVE-2025-29927: x-middleware-subrequest made Next skip middleware entirely on self-hosted apps
        - label The bypass class survives the patch
          desc Header smuggling, proxy misrouting, a matcher gap, or the next CVE all skip the same single door
        - label A layout check runs once, gates nothing
          desc Persists across client navigation (misses revoked sessions) and renders in parallel with the page's fetches
        - label redirect() is a UX courtesy, not a boundary
          desc Usually fires, never guaranteed — segments are individually addressable, bypassing the wrapper
    - label Data Access Layer (check at every read)
      children
        - label The check is the path
          desc Every query starts with verifySession — no route can reach a row without passing it
        - label cache(): 1 lookup per request
          desc Memoized verifySession — ten DAL calls cost one ~1-2 ms KV lookup, not ten
        - label Per-row authorization, not just authn
          desc ownerId === session.userId before return — blocks horizontal privilege escalation
        - label Returns a DTO, never the raw row
          desc Ships only the fields the UI needs, so no client component can leak unintended columns
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
